Z||000000||Mach10||07-22-2001||05:58 PM||||Just about have my Beast running perfect EXCEPT that it can be a REAL pain to start sometimes. Syptoms: Won't catch right away, can take up to 12 cranks to get going. Then it sounds like it's running on 3 cylinders for 3-4 seconds. Then it smooths out and no more issues. I checked the exhaust, no smoke. Just rump-rump-rump-rump-rumparumpa-rummmmmmmmmmmmm....<BR>No codes, plugs/wires changed. Confused? Very. Any suggestions?<BR>||||reg||7
Z||000001||JayUSA77||07-22-2001||06:56 PM||||my only ideas is that your starter isnt strong enough to crank over your size engine, or the battery doesnt have a full charge to crank the starter over.<BR>J<P>------------------<BR>86' Black Fiero GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||Mach10||07-22-2001||06:59 PM||||If you disconnect the coil, it'll crank nice and hard for as long as you'd want. It doesn't even slow down. HOWEVER, it seems to me like the spark is weak. I'm thinking either my battery is flocked, or my coil is going. I figure that if a cell is blown on the battery, then it'll put out the juice needed to crank, and fire, but not well. Am I grasping at straws?||||reg||8
Z||000003||JayUSA77||07-22-2001||07:05 PM||||Well first check your acid level in your battery. Take off those tabs on top of your batter and fill them with spring water if low.  and your right if the coil is going bad it would take a while to kick over but then it also feel kinda weak.  Does your car drive fine even when you get on it.?<BR>J<P>------------------<BR>86' Black Fiero GT||||reg||1
